WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.467
A market headline leaves important questions unanswered.

2
00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:08.367
Sourcebrief preserves the evidence behind the headline.

3
00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:12.067
Inspect, save, compare, and export.

4
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:16.967
These are genuine Panta responses, replayed locally.

5
00:00:16.967 --> 00:00:20.067
They were captured on October second.

6
00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:23.533
The original time and recorded label remain.

7
00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:27.367
Missing catalogue titles come from retrieved detail.

8
00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:32.200
Read the resolution wording beside its sources.

9
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.000
Source identifiers are supplied by the provider.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.333
They are not independently verified links.

11
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:43.467
Missing or shortened information stays explicitly marked.

12
00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:48.867
Price source and status remain visible.

13
00:00:48.867 --> 00:00:52.267
Undocumented raw scales are not guessed.

14
00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:56.133
Zero is a value, not missing information.

15
00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:59.967
Reported and total volume remain separate fields.

16
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:06.167
Save this observation as a local checkpoint.

17
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.967
It stays attached to this market.

18
00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:12.200
The original capture time travels with it.

19
00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:19.267
This capture shows the checkpoint after reload.

20
00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:22.867
Persistence belongs to this browser and origin.

21
00:01:22.867 --> 00:01:25.967
It is not an immutable audit log.

22
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:32.567
Refresh compares supported fields with that checkpoint.

23
00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:36.567
Replaying the same observation changes no facts.

24
00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:40.200
A new request identifier is not change.

25
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.400
Equivalent decimal formatting also remains unchanged.

26
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:49.533
Export a readable brief or structured JSON.

27
00:01:49.533 --> 00:01:52.933
Both preserve source mode and capture time.

28
00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:57.433
Changed fields retain before and after values.

29
00:01:57.433 --> 00:02:01.600
This is a reviewable handoff, not certification.

30
00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.933
This captured record reports a resolved outcome.

31
00:02:05.933 --> 00:02:09.200
Its zero and one values stay intact.

32
00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.100
They are not current trading quotes.

33
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.133
Independently implemented, with substantial Codex assistance.

34
00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:23.267
Optional live mode uses your own key.

35
00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:26.933
No trading or independent source certification.

36
00:02:26.933 --> 00:02:30.300
External adoption has not yet been measured.

37
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.767
Inspect the code and reproducible evidence.

